   },
   "evidence": "agent-test.ts:129-136: when the 1 s HTTP attempt times out, the code calls `await second(body, signal)`, and the socket's connection error replaces the timeout. gate-slot.ts:152 then applies `if ((first && !(e instanceof DaemonTimeoutError)) || clock.now() - lastReply > GATE_LEASE_EXPIRY_MS) throw ... unreachable`, and that unreachable error falls through to `warn(e)` and `work()`, so the command runs unslotted. lastReply only moves on a reply that arrives in time (line 149). Normally slotted.ts creates the socket and serves it from the same daemon, so the first path needs the socket to be missing or blocked. The 30 s silence rule was already in base gate-slot.ts; this change newly applies it to agent tests, although the design doc says the wrapper falls back to unslotted only when confinement denies both transports."
