   "evidence": "HEAD's wrapper first uses `bounded(..., 1000)`, then executes `const reply = await second(body, signal)` after any non-LeaseRejected error. A socket refusal therefore replaces the HTTP timeout. In gate-slot.ts, `(first && !(e instanceof DaemonTimeoutError))` classifies that replacement as unreachable, and the outer catch warns before executing work. Independently, `lastReply = clock.now()` runs only after a timely request result, so late replies cannot prevent the 30000ms silence fallback. Base already had the silence rule, but had neither this wrapper nor its timeout-masking transport fallback. The later commit preserves DaemonTimeoutError across fallback, observes late replies, and disables silence-based unslotted execution for agent commands."
