   "failure_scenario": "Suppose an agent's test suite loses its lease because heartbeats stalled for 30 s, and the reply to the wrapper's recovery request is then slow. The service rejects the wrapper's retry, heartbeats stop for good, and the slot frees while the suite is still running, so a second suite can start beside it.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/f2/f2.test.ts: a throwaway test that runs withGateLease with the agentTest option against a real AgentTestSession and fake clock. It blocks all requests for 45 s, then holds the first recovery reply (once ignoring the abort, once honouring it the way fetch does).",
    "output": "after blackout occupied=0\nrecovery processed, reply held\nrejected recovery: Error: running recovery requires an earlier heartbeat-expired lease of this invocation\nafter retries occupied=1\nlate recovery reply delivered\n45s later, work still running, occupied=0\nother invocation acquired=true\n(same result with the abort honoured; 2 pass)"
   },
   "evidence": "agent-tests.ts:132-138 rejects any recovery unless `previous.status === \"heartbeat\"`, but line 163 has already set `previous.status = \"recovered\"` before the reply is sent. On the wrapper side (gate-slot.ts:182), `if (!stopped && !(opts.agentTest && e instanceof LeaseRejected)) beat(1000);` stops heartbeating after the rejected retry. When a late reply does arrive, lines 95-97 adopt the new id, but nothing calls beat() again. In wrapperLeaseClient the HTTP attempt gives up after 1 s and retries the same recovery over the socket, so a recovery that takes over 1 s is enough to trigger this."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A running test suite renews its expired reservation, but the renewal response is delayed. Retries stop maintaining the replacement reservation, allowing another suite to start while the first suite is still running.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-f2.ts\"",
    "output": "Using the real AgentTestSession and Semaphore with fake time: at 34000ms the delayed replacement lease was adopted, occupancy was 1, and work remained running; warnings included the recovery timeout and rejected retry. At 62000ms occupancy had fallen to 0 while the first work remained running, and a second invocation acquired the lane."
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD marks the old lease `previous.status = \"recovered\"` before returning its replacement, but recovery requires `previous.status !== \"heartbeat\"` to be false. Retrying the old lease therefore rejects. The wrapper's catch schedules another heartbeat only when `!(opts.agentTest && e instanceof LeaseRejected)`, so this rejection stops renewal. A late reply still updates the lease ID, but that adoption does not restart heartbeats. Base had no AgentTestSession recovery restriction, and its heartbeat catch unconditionally retried while work remained active. The later commit records the replacement registration for idempotent recovery retries and calls `beat()` when adopting a recovery response."
  }
